From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Description: Relax ANGLE ResourceMap static_assert to fix FTBFS with GCC 12
 GCC 12 evaluates the static_assert inside the discarded branch of
 "if constexpr (kAdditionalFlatResourcesSize > 0)" when instantiating
 ResourceMap<>::assignAboveCurrentFlatSize, failing the build with
 "static assertion failed" at ResourceMap.h:463.  Newer compilers
 (clang, GCC >= 13) skip discarded branches as required, so this only
 affects architectures building WebKit with GCC 12 such as loong64.
 .
 Rewrite the assertion as an equivalent expression that also holds when
 the additional flat resources are disabled; when the branch is
 genuinely taken the invariant (kAdditionalFlatResourcesSize > 0
 requires kNeedsLock) is still enforced.
Forwarded: no
---

--- a/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/src/libANGLE/ResourceMap.h
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/src/libANGLE/ResourceMap.h
@@ -460,7 +460,7 @@ void ResourceMap<ResourceType, IDType>::assignAboveCurrentFlatSize(GLuint handle
     {
         // This should only possible when lock is needed. Otherwise we could just grow
         // mFlatResources.
-        static_assert(kNeedsLock);
+        static_assert(kAdditionalFlatResourcesSize == 0 || kNeedsLock);
         if (handle < kLocklessFlatResourcesLimit)
         {
             ResourceType **additionalResources =
